{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Speak… and they shall turn back…</b> Behold, anyone who sees this will be puzzled: why should HaShem need to devise a stratagem, heaven forbid, in this matter, when He can do whatever He pleases in the heart of Pharaoh to pursue?" "<b>Truly,</b> when one reflects upon what has preceded us regarding knowledge of the attribute of the Creator — that He desires for the sake of vindicating Israel — is not this the matter that HaShem spoke in this commandment: that He devised a plan so that they would not stumble in provoking the Creator and say words of blasphemy, such as they said afterward (Exodus 14:11): ״הַמִבְּלִי אֵין קְבָרִים… הֲלֹא… טוֹב לָנוּ עֲבֹד אֶת מִצְרַיִם״ etc. And HaShem devised a plan and did a thing tangible and manifest to them — that HaShem counseled evil against Pharaoh and devised a plan against him to bring him out of Egypt to pursue Israel, so as to exact retribution upon him. From this point on, there is no room for Israel to fear Pharaoh; on the contrary, they will anticipate his approach to see their vengeance upon him. And it did not suffice for the Creator to tell them these things by word of mouth alone — that He would harden Pharaoh's heart to pursue them — for they would not be impressed by these things; but upon seeing him, they would quake and be inclined to turn back to him out of fear of him. Therefore HaShem commanded that they turn back and encamp and perform the action that would prepare the way for Pharaoh to pursue them, and this thing would impress them and make an impact upon them — for they themselves would be the ones making the preparation, with a felt and stirring awareness, that they turned back behind them and encamped in a designated place from which Pharaoh would be misled into pursuing them; and through this their hearts would not despair, and when he came, יָגֵל יַעֲקֹב יִשְׂמַח יִשְׂרָאֵל — for he would behold vengeance upon his enemy. And you will find that even so it did not help absolutely. Go out and learn from what they said upon seeing him, and from this you may infer what they would have done without the turning back. Understand."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:27:45.158203845Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}